.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt CMS_ENVELOPEDDATA_CREATE 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm CMS_EnvelopedData_create_ex ,
.Nm CMS_EnvelopedData_create ,
.Nm CMS_AuthEnvelopedData_create ,
.Nm CMS_AuthEnvelopedData_create_ex
.Nd Create CMS envelope
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/cms.h
.Ft CMS_ContentInfo *

.Fo CMS_EnvelopedData_create_ex
.Fa "const EVP_CIPHER *cipher"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Ft CMS_ContentInfo *
.Fo CMS_EnvelopedData_create
.Fa "const EVP_CIPHER *cipher"
.Fc
.Ft CMS_ContentInfo *

.Fo CMS_AuthEnvelopedData_create_ex
.Fa "const EVP_CIPHER *cipher"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Ft CMS_ContentInfo *
.Fo CMS_AuthEnvelopedData_create
.Fa "const EVP_CIPHER *cipher"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn CMS_EnvelopedData_create_ex
creates a
.Vt CMS_ContentInfo
structure with a type
.Sy NID_pkcs7_enveloped .
.Fa cipher
is the symmetric cipher to use.
The library context
.Fa libctx
and the property query
.Fa propq
are used when retrieving algorithms from providers.
.Pp
.Fn CMS_AuthEnvelopedData_create_ex
creates a
.Vt CMS_ContentInfo
structure with a type
.Sy NID_id_smime_ct_authEnvelopedData .
.Fa cipher
is the symmetric AEAD cipher to use.
Currently only AES variants with GCM mode are supported.
The library context
.Fa libctx
and the property query
.Fa propq
are used when retrieving algorithms from providers.
.Pp
The algorithm passed in the
.Fa cipher
parameter must support ASN1 encoding of its parameters.
.Pp
The recipients can be added later using
.Xr CMS_add1_recipient_cert 3
or
.Xr CMS_add0_recipient_key 3 .
.Pp
The
.Vt CMS_ContentInfo
structure needs to be finalized using
.Xr CMS_final 3
and then freed using
.Xr CMS_ContentInfo_free 3 .
.Pp
.Fn CMS_EnvelopedData_create
and
.Fn CMS_AuthEnvelopedData_create
are similar to
.Fn CMS_EnvelopedData_create_ex
and
.Fn CMS_AuthEnvelopedData_create_ex
but use default values of NULL for the library context
.Fa libctx
and the property query
.Fa propq .
.Sh NOTES
Although
.Fn CMS_EnvelopedData_create_ex ,
and
.Fn CMS_EnvelopedData_create ,
.Fn CMS_AuthEnvelopedData_create_ex ,
and
.Fn CMS_AuthEnvelopedData_create
allocate a new
.Vt CMS_ContentInfo
structure, they are not usually used in applications.
The wrappers
.Xr CMS_encrypt 3
and
.Xr CMS_decrypt 3
are often used instead.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
If the allocation fails,
.Fn CMS_EnvelopedData_create_ex ,
.Fn CMS_EnvelopedData_create ,
.Fn CMS_AuthEnvelopedData_create_ex ,
.Fn CMS_AuthEnvelopedData_create ,
.Fn CMS_AuthEnvelopedData_create ,
and
.Fn CMS_AuthEnvelopedData_create_ex
return NULL and set an error code that can be obtained by
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 .
Otherwise, they return a pointer to the newly allocated structure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 ,
.Xr CMS_encrypt 3 ,
.Xr CMS_decrypt 3 ,
.Xr CMS_final 3 ,
.Xr CMS_sign_ex 3 ,
.Xr CMS_encrypt_ex 3
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn CMS_EnvelopedData_create_ex
method was added in OpenSSL 3.0.
.Pp
.Fn CMS_AuthEnvelopedData_create
and
.Fn CMS_AuthEnvelopedData_create_ex
were added in OpenSSL 3.5.
